&lt;p&gt;Mercury* is building a complete financial stack for ambitious businesses. Since we launched in 2019, our customer base has grown to over 200,000 startups and small businesses from all around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within the Revenue Strategy &amp;amp; Operations group, the Platforms &amp;amp; Infrastructure team owns the systems, workflows, and processes that power Mercury&#39;s revenue organization across Sales, Partnerships, and Account Management. Our revenue org has grown past 100 sellers and is on a path to more than double. At that scale, our systems are how we change behavior and drive efficiency, and AI is fundamentally rewriting how these systems get built. We&#39;re looking for a leader to take advantage of that shift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;*Mercury is a fintech company, not an FDIC-insured bank. Banking services provided through Choice Financial Group and Column N.A., Members FDIC.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As Head of Revenue Technology, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy and execution for the systems, workflows, and processes that power Mercury&#39;s revenue organization, serving three teams with distinct needs: Sales, Partnerships, and Account Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take business problems, design solutions, and ship them fast. We iterate in weeks, not quarters, and we&#39;d rather put something imperfect in front of users and improve it than wait for the perfect build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rebuild our revenue stack AI-first, both in what we ship (automation, scoring, agent-driven workflows) and in how we build it (using AI to do the development itself).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a hands-on builder. You&#39;ll bring a strong point of view, get into the work, and actively shape and design solutions alongside your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate fluently between business and technical. You&#39;ll deeply understand what the revenue org is trying to accomplish, then flip gears and architect how to get there.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and grow a tenured team of admins, engineers, and architects, guiding them to a high-speed, iterative operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver value on top of imperfect foundations, while improving those foundations over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and leverage strong stakeholder and partner relationships to build consensus and drive impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;There are lots of paths that could lead you to be successful in a role like this; we think the strongest candidates will have some of this experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years working in and around revenue systems, GTM systems, or revenue architecture in a B2B environment, ideally at a revenue org of 250+ sellers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years managing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a product-led company with a sales or revenue motion layered on top.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of taking a business problem end to end: ingest it, design the solution, implement it, and do it quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience deploying AI into GTM systems. If you&#39;ve rebuilt an AI-powered GTM stack, that&#39;s our gold standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce fluency is useful, but your career doesn’t need to be defined by it. We&#39;re looking for people who took the non-standard route: product managers, systems builders, operators who taught themselves the technical side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven change leadership: you&#39;ve brought experienced teams through significant shifts in how they work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong conviction and communication skills, with the ability to influence senior leaders while staying close to the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
