&lt;p&gt;In 1945, elevator operators walked out of New York&#39;s office buildings. The city ground to a halt with millions of workers stuck on the street and a hundred million in losses. Automatic elevators had existed since the 1890s. Nobody would ride one without a person at the controls. It took the strike, and the decade after it, building trust car by car, building by building, before people would step into a box and press a button themselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mercury, we build for the building class: the people who see something that doesn&#39;t exist and decide to make it real — with their time, their money, their team. Whether that&#39;s a side project or a scaling unicorn, we build the financial stack that gets them there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the future of financial software is infrastructure that works on your behalf. We’re looking for a product leader to accelerate our AI bets – Command, CLI, MCP – and our API as we build towards a Mercury that is programmable and intelligent. This is a role for a builder who is capable across the stack with hands-on experience building with AI.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;*Mercury is a fintech company, not an FDIC-insured bank. Banking services provided through Choice Financial Group and Column N.A., Members FDIC.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As part of the journey, we would expect you to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of how Mercury&#39;s most technical customers use our product today, and what they&#39;re trying to do that they can&#39;t yet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the product vision for how our AI products – Command, CLI, MCP – transform the way people interact with their finance stack: from asking questions about their business to taking action on their behalf&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Mercury&#39;s strategy for connecting to the broader ecosystem of AI tools; build and automate the workflow end to end using Command, CLI, MCP, and the rest of our AI stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap for Mercury&#39;s API and drive it from niche, read-heavy usage toward a comprehensive platform that enables customers to build on top of Mercury&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering to make hard technical tradeoffs about interfaces, API design, data access, and capabilities: you should be able to hold your own in these conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Mercury&#39;s growth and partnerships teams to ensure our AI products are a competitive advantage in acquisition and retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate a high-velocity environment where leadership cares deeply about this space and expects you to move fast and think originally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some things that might make you successful in a role like this:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re genuinely excited about what&#39;s happening in AI right now and are actively building with these tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong opinions about AI products and the judgment to recognize fast when one of them is wrong. You&#39;re not waiting for someone to tell you what&#39;s possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience building — as a founder or product manager — including meaningful time owning product decisions end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be dangerous across the stack and able to grapple directly with complex concepts; hands on experience building AI products with AI, and knowledge about RAG, evals, agent harnesses a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand what it means to build for developers and technical users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in a culture where leadership is deeply engaged&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can take a nascent product area with real traction and turn it into a coherent strategy with a clear roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn more about what we&#39;re building:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
